9. Future-date guard: registrationDate after server date → `FutureRegistrationDateException`.
10. Effective date = registrationDate or today, then `businessDayResolver.toBusinessDay(...)` rolls weekend→Monday; stored as `registrationDate`.
11. `countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate)`; if `>= 100` → `OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`.
12. Set `bulkSignupWarning = (count > 80)`.
13. `countOwnersInCity(city)`; if `>= 50` → `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`.
14. If postcode present: set `householdId = householdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode)` (SHA-256 hex prefix).
15. `findOwnersByIdentityKey(owner.getIdentityKey())` non-empty → `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (identityKey = `telephone|email|householdId`).
16. `findHouseholdDuplicateOf(owner)` non-null AND `sharesHousehold != true` → `DuplicateHouseholdException`.
17. `saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) — for new owner sets, in order: `customerCode` (region + SHA hash), `namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber` (customerCode + reg-year), `householdSize`; then `ownerRepository.save`.
18. `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` — AUDIT log line.
19. Map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return `201 CREATED`.

One caveat worth flagging: steps 11/13/15/16 each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` and stream-filter in memory (no dedicated query methods used), and there is no unique DB constraint enforcing the duplicate checks — the duplicate/limit checks are read-then-write without locking, so they are racy under concurrency.
